  "preconditions": [
    "12.s.W: Validated code_ref and an explicit native ProjectBoundary or already bound GitObjectSource. Expected hashes, exact stored selectors and historical commits are supplied by owned fixtures.",
    "12.s.R: An already admitted native file or immutable GitObjectSource capability. Real local SHA-1/SHA-256 object stores, exact record selectors and owned faults; no substitute source is created when admission fails."
  ],
  "steps": [
    "12.s.W: Assess original file hashes and exact H.2 line/text/byte selections. Preserve current at the stored position despite outside changes/duplicate matches; report one relocation without rewriting. Observe absent file/Git paths, distinguish absent and ambiguous selections, retain source/selector failures and check detached reports. Recheck missing-path/root/store boundaries and exercise fresh audited Core/PYZ runtimes.",
    "12.s.R: Cross every H.3 selection outcome with both raw-hash results and native file/SHA-1/SHA-256 sources. Remove bound commits, root/parent trees and blobs for every reference kind; assert missing without fabricated hashes. Corrupt objects, inject malformed/failed batch responses, reject unsafe parents, preserve read errors and verify exact stale reasons for empty/truncated/overlapping/Unicode/newline cases. Retain old reader errors, forbid fetch/fallback and audit fresh Core/PYZ Git reads."
  ],
  "oracle": {
    "kind": "behavior",
    "requirement_contract": "Der Code-Referenzzustand MUSS ausschließlich durch die disjunkte Tabelle in Anhang H.3 bestimmt werden.",
    "scope": "The first applicable H.3 rule yields one state. Absent admitted paths are missing/target_missing; file hash equality decides current versus stale/file_changed. Stored selection equality takes precedence over raw-file changes and other matches. Unique alternate matches relocate without writes; zero/multiple matches are stale with selection_missing/selection_ambiguous. Safety, source and decoding failures are not currency. The immutable projection binds original references and available source/location reports; no approval or write authority is conferred. 12.s.R completes the matrix over admitted sources. Only exact native batch absence of the requested full Git object ID is missing. Object content/type/size/identity, response shape, original root/store and safe parent traversal remain mandatory. Corruption, process failure and body/open/read errors yield no state; the original strict readers and source constructor keep their contracts."
  },
